From 26d643fd3ab2607715410fc65b9507c898612383 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 21:28:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(work+map): give every job a page, and the map a legend
 that names it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two halves of the same problem.

1. The portfolio cards went nowhere. /portfolio rendered nine <article>
   elements with a photo, a headline and a card shadow, and no
   /portfolio/{slug} route existed to click through to. The catalogue
   deep-linked to #slug fragments, site search returned nine results that all
   resolved to the same grid, and every "related work" card on the homepage,
   the service pages, the service x city pages and the area pages had the
   same dead end. Nothing was broken, so nothing caught it.

   Ships nine statically generated job pages (ISR 1h, own canonical,
   breadcrumbs, CreativeWork JSON-LD whose ImageObject creditText says the
   photograph is an illustrative rendering — no rating, no review, no
   customer), and makes every card that renders a project a real link.

   The grid uses a stretched link rather than an anchor wrapped around the
   card, because three cards contain a before/after slider and a slider
   inside an anchor cannot be dragged. The slider is lifted above the
   overlay instead. Verified in a browser: photo click navigates, body copy
   navigates, slider drags 52 -> 79 without navigating.

   Also fixes components/before-after.tsx, which used a literal id and so
   put three elements with the same DOM id on /portfolio.

2. The map showed where the shop works but not what it does there. Rebuilt
   with a stats header card, a control column (zoom / reset / full screen)
   and a collapsible legend that NAMES its four statuses — studio, core
   service area, extended range, worked example — each with a clause saying
   what it means. Status is encoded by shape as well as colour; adds
   --color-map-extended (#a8742a) because --color-primary and --color-accent
   are both greens and core-versus-travel is the map's most commercial
   distinction. Worked examples pulse, carry a count badge where a
   municipality has more than one, and every popup ends in a real CTA button.

   CoverageMap now takes a serviceSlug, so the stairs page shows stair
   municipalities and stair examples, installation shows install, and so on.
   The filter reads CatalogEntry.serviceSlug off the job types each
   municipality is offered, so it cannot drift from tierNote()'s prose.
   Maps placed on the homepage (380px, compact), /areas, all 32 area pages,
   all 8 service pages, all 224 service x city pages and /stairs.

Honesty: data/coverage.ts still may not import data/projects.ts — the
photography is AI-generated and pinning it at real locations would put
invented work at checkable addresses. The join lives in data/showcase.ts
under three rules tests/showcase.test.ts pins: municipality precision only
(strict-equal to the centroid, drawn as a hollow ring), illustrative: true
with a disclosure rendered in the legend, the popup and server HTML, and no
customer/date/quote/rating field on the type. confirmedJobs stays empty.

MapWorkedExamples renders the same list as real <a> elements under every
map, because the client legend does not exist for a crawler.

Evidence: 290 tests pass (263 before). 393 prerendered pages (384 before).
Site audit clean — no broken links, no duplicate titles, zero warnings.
Playwright across six viewports and ten routes: no horizontal overflow.
Leaflet stays out of the shared bundle (own async chunk, IntersectionObserver
gated); shared bundle unchanged at 103 kB. Dropped the unused `note` field
from the serialised map payload.

